-- title:
--   Decoding Fermat-ring residues back into Gaussian-integer blocks
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a list of $N$ canonical residues modulo $F = 2^{4rP}+1$ on stack `XD`, $l \le 4rP$, and let the registers hold $N$, $2^{4rP-l}$, $2^{4rP}$, $F$, $2^P$, $r$. For $W\ge 2\cdot 4rP+3$, $W\ge\mathrm{zsz}(N)$, $Q\ge P$, $Q \ge \mathrm{zsz}(r)$, the program `dcL` consumes $C$ and pushes on `KO` the (reversed) concatenation of `decBlk F P r` applied to each scaled residue `scl (4rP) l c` $= c\cdot 2^{2\cdot4rP-l} \bmod F$, within cost `dcCost N r P Q W`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `decBlk` (unpacking a residue into $r$ Gaussian integers with signed $P$-bit digits) is from `Def_IntMul_HvdH_MachineRef`. The machine layer: `IState HS` is a state with $64$ stacks of items (`Item` = integer or mark), an input position and an output; `RM` programs (straight-line register code `RS`, loops `rep`, conditionals, calls of the multiplication procedure through a `MulSpec` $M$ giving its domain and cost) have a functional semantics `p.run s`, a definedness predicate `p.ok M s` and a cost `p.cost M s`; `Spec M p s s' c` abbreviates `p.ok M s ∧ p.run s = s' ∧ p.cost M s ≤ c`. `ints L` / `gints U` push an integer list / a list of pairs as items (head = top); `zsz z` is the bit length of $|z|$. `MulBnd M m Φ` says the multiplication procedure accepts all pairs of integers of bit length $\le m$ at cost $\le Φ$. Register names (`GU`, `CR`, `KB`, `XN`, …) are fixed stack indices.
-- source:
--   D. Harvey, J. van der Hoeven, Integer multiplication in time O(n log n), Ann. of Math. 193 (2021), 563–617 (Theorem 1.1: multitape Turing machine multiplication in O(n log n)). Lemma `NLogN.FW.dcL_spec` of the Lean development NLogN/HFW8.lean (lines 158–230), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

